    <bpmn:process id="W_W4669" name="W4669. Cost-Accounting Calendar, Period Close &amp; Cost Allocation Cycles" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Cost-accounting calendar; period close
Frequency: Monthly (+ weekly flash for volatile categories)
Volume: 5 entities × 12 months; multiple allocation cycles
Owner: Cost Accounting Manager
Participants: Controller, GL/Close (VS-17.1), DC Ops (VS-04), HR (VS-19)
Source: workflow W4669 — Cost-Accounting Calendar, Period Close &amp; Cost Allocation Cycles</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W4669_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W4669_Lane1" name="Cost Accounting">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4669_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4669_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4669_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4669_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W4669_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W4669_Start3" name="Cost-accounting calendar; period close">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4669_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4669_Task4" name="Maintain the cost-accounting calendar aligned to the fiscal close (W9A/W9B)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Maintain the cost-accounting calendar aligned to the fiscal close (W9A/W9B): standard-cost roll, landed-cost run, freight/duty allocation, overhead absorption, variance analysis, NRV review — sequenced with dependencies
Responsible (R): Cost Accounting / GL
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: Per calendar</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4669_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4669_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4669_Task5" name="Execute the cost-allocation cycles each period: freight/handling to SKU…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Execute the cost-allocation cycles each period: freight/handling to SKU (W4652), overhead to product/service, labor to service/project (W4666), IC cost transfer (W4667); post and reconcile each cycle
Responsible (R): Cost Accounting
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: Per close</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4669_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4669_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W4669_Task6" name="Validate the cost close before financial-close sign-off: all variances posted…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Validate the cost close before financial-close sign-off: all variances posted, COGS reconciled (W4663), margin pack produced (W4661); resolve exceptions
Responsible (R): Cost Accounting / GL
Accountable (A): Controller
Duration: Per close</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W4669_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W4669_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W4669_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W4669_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W4669_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-706 (ensure controlled execution — Specialized Costing (Project, Service, Intercompany) &amp; Cost Governance (PA-158.3).) | - CTL-706: cost calendar sequenced with dependencies; allocation cycles posted and reconciled; close validated before sign-off
Owner: Cost Accounting Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
